  "es419": { "note": "The rule is the same in Latin America. Quiero que vayáis is Spain only: there people say quiero que vayan." },
  "subtitle": "Ask who does the second action. The same person: use the infinitive (Quiero ir). A different person: use que + subjunctive (Quiero que vayas). Don't say Quiero que yo vaya.",
  "briefMarks": ["quiero ir", "quiero que vayas", "que", "infinitive", "subjunctive"],
  "source": "icanspeak Spanish original text (grammar-b1 run, 2026-11-04)",
  "concept": {
    "comic": {
      "title": "¿Quién {sale}?",
      "panels": [
        {
          "caption": "Same person",
          "tag": "{quiero} + infinitive",
          "left": { "name": "regi", "expr": "thinking", "say": "¿Qué quieres hacer esta noche?" },
          "right": { "name": "quaki", "expr": "happy", "say": "{Quiero} {salir}." }
        },
        {
          "caption": "Different people",
          "tag": "{quiero que} + subjunctive",
          "left": { "name": "bruno", "expr": "thinking", "say": "¿Y yo? ¿Me quedo en casa?" },
          "right": { "name": "quaki", "expr": "celebrate", "say": "¡No! {Quiero que} {salgas} conmigo." }
        },
        {
          "caption": "In general or for one person",
          "tag": "{es importante} + infinitive, {es importante que} + subjunctive",
          "left": { "name": "hamsti", "expr": "thinking", "say": "{Es importante} {pedir} cita." },
          "right": { "name": "regi", "expr": "happy", "say": "Y {es importante que} {lleves} el pasaporte." }
        }
      ]
    },
    "flow": [
      { "text": "same person: quiero" },
      { "text": "ir", "variant": "verb" },
      { "text": "different person: quiero que", "variant": "prep" },
      { "text": "vayas", "variant": "verb" }
    ],
    "exampleHtml": "Quiero <span class=\"vp-verb\">ir</span> al médico. · <span class=\"vp-prep\">Quiero que</span> <span class=\"vp-verb\">vayas</span> al médico. · Necesito <span class=\"vp-verb\">descansar</span>. · <span class=\"vp-prep\">Necesito que</span> me <span class=\"vp-verb\">ayudes</span>.",
    "qa": [
      {
        "html": "<strong>One person does both things:</strong> use the infinitive. <em>(Yo) quiero (yo) trabajar → Quiero trabajar.</em> <em>Ana quiere estudiar.</em>",
        "tag": "Same person"
      },
      {
        "html": "<strong>Two different people:</strong> use <em>que</em> + subjunctive. <em>Quiero que trabajes</em> = I want you to work. <em>Ana quiere que estudiemos</em> = Ana wants us to study.",
        "tag": "Different people"
      },
      {
        "html": "The same pattern works with feelings: <em>Me gusta cocinar</em> (I cook) and <em>Me gusta que cocines</em> (you cook). <em>Me alegra verte</em> and <em>Me alegra que vengas</em>.",
        "tag": "Feelings"
      },
      {
        "html": "<strong>es importante, es necesario, es mejor</strong>: use the infinitive for people in general, and <em>que</em> + subjunctive for a particular person. <em>Es importante pedir cita. Es importante que pidas cita.</em>",
        "tag": "General or personal"
      },
      {
        "html": "With the same person, <em>que</em> is wrong in Spanish, even if you can say <em>I want that</em> in your language. <em>Quiero que vaya</em> means someone else goes: he, she or usted.",
        "tag": "Careful"
      }
    ],
    "noteHtml": "Common mistakes: ✗ <em>Quiero que yo vaya</em> → ✓ <em>Quiero ir</em>. ✗ <em>Quiero tú vas</em> → ✓ <em>Quiero que vayas</em>. ✗ <em>Quiero ir tú</em> → ✓ <em>Quiero que vayas</em>. ✗ <em>Necesito que descanso</em> → ✓ <em>Necesito descansar</em>.",
    "reference": {
      "showLabel": "Show overview ▼",
      "hideLabel": "Hide overview ▲",
